cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference MYCEL in academic work, please cite this specification."
title: "MYCEL: A Continuous Reactive Field Topology Language for Embodied AI, Neuro-Evolution and Tensor Fields"
abstract: >-
  MYCEL is a programming language design in which a program is a ledger of fields rather
  than a sequence of instructions. Execution is non-sequential: fields are resolved on
  monotone frontiers across independent clock domains. The language provides structural
  reverse-mode automatic differentiation, native evolutionary operators on topology, a
  spatial geometry type system with named axes and SI unit algebra, and a static memory
  model with zero steady-state allocations. The surface syntax is restricted to the 94
  printable ASCII code points.
